IMPORT prelude

-- Customs Securities (Penalties) Act 1981 (Cth). Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A02424.txt. Seat: the tenderer.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Security case` HAS
    `tender accepted`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `refused or failed to give security when required`  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(1): set out in the undertaking, as a percentage
    `prescribed percentage`                             IS A NUMBER
    -- s 3(2): a unit value in the undertaking, if any
    `value per unit`                                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `units`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `value of the goods`                                IS A NUMBER

§ `Rules`

@ref s 3(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Security case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of the goods for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `value per unit`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN c's `value of the goods`
    WHEN JUST v  THEN v TIMES c's `units`

@ref s 4
@export default The penalty I owe under s 4 of the Customs Securities (Penalties) Act 1981 (Cth) for refusing or failing to give security when a Collector required it, after my tender was accepted: the prescribed percentage set out in my Customs undertaking of the value of the goods (at the undertaking's unit value, if it sets one). Nil otherwise. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Security case`  @desc The tender, the failure to give security, the prescribed percentage and the goods' value
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my security penalty for` c MEANS
    IF c's `tender accepted` AND c's `refused or failed to give security when required`
    THEN c's `prescribed percentage` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `the value of the goods for` c
    ELSE 0
